        ".²1 The god of riches and treasure and the regent of the northern quarter;\n {#kuberaguptAM diSamuzRaraSmO gantuM pravftte samayaM vilaNGya#} <ls>Ku. 3. 25</ls>\n ({%vide%} <ls>Malli.</ls> thereon). [Kubera is the son of Viśravas by Iḍāviḍā,\n and thus the half brother of Rāvaṇa. Besides, being the lord of riches\n and regent of the north, he is the king of the Yakṣas and Kinnaras, and\n a friend of Rudra. His abode is Kailāsa. He is represented as being deformed\n in body-having three legs, only eight teeth, and a yellow mark in place of one eye.]\n",
        ".²2 <ab>N.</ab> of a tree.\n"
